    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for LawDog hinges on exploiting high-upside matchups against back-end starters, with **Bryson Stott** and **Geraldo Perdomo** anchoring the offense as our strongest plays. Both players benefit from favorable matchups against R. V\u00e1squez and Eric Lauer respectively, carrying scores north of 72.0. **Stott**\u2019s projection is bolstered by a significant 18% SP skill advantage and a strong platoon edge, while **Perdomo**\u2014a key cog in our focus on speed\u2014benefits from a 16% SP skill advantage against the lefty Lauer. We are also looking for a breakout performance from **Lawrence Butler** (68.09) and **Tyler Freeman** (68.64); both remain in the starting nine as the optimizer rewards their strong platoon positioning and high-leverage order spots, despite the risk associated with pending lineups.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was leaving **Jung Hoo Lee** (38.92) and **Masyn Winn** (38.85) out of the active roster. **Jung Hoo Lee** was the closest to cracking the lineup, but a negative platoon split against the lefty Kyle Harrison effectively capped his efficiency below our 40-point threshold. Similarly, **Masyn Winn** fell just short of the floor, penalized heavily by a negative park factor and an elite 3.29 xERA opposing starter in Nathan Eovaldi. Elsewhere, we are monitoring the wind report for **Daulton Varsho**, whose 60.04 score is excellent but tempered by a 5% penalty for wind blowing in, and **Lawrence Butler**, who faces a similar atmospheric hurdle. While **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (56.49) remains a high-floor start, his score is surprisingly suppressed today by a 19% negative SP skill adjustment, reminding us that even our anchors must navigate tough matchups. We continue to hold **Cal Raleigh** on the IL, awaiting his return to bolster the catching depth currently occupied by **Will Smith**.",
